  "protocol": "Separate process per budget, profile and instrumentation mode. Both timing arms use the same Release llama-server, standard expert and prefill profiles, single slot, BF16 KV. Only the candidate sets LLAMA_LFM_GQA4=1. Sequential Metal runs. Warm 15 -> 8 and 4000 -> 8, then three uncached 4000 -> 64 requests, independently greedy. TTFT and request time are measured on client SSE events, excluding server startup. Decode TPS = 63/(time from first to last token event). Columns are independent medians. Timing arm order alternates by budget.",
  "logit_protocol": "A separate diagnostic server evaluates the two kernels on the exact same input IDs at all 64 output positions. After storing every FP32 vocabulary logit and the independently sampled ID it supplies the fixture reference token as the next input. Row 0 is the final prompt position and rows 1..63 are serial decode. Hashes cover the full matrices in row-major order. A Metal encode-site counter counts actual GQA4 dispatches in this request. Errors and top-1 agreement are computed on all 64 x 128000 logits at each budget. Clean timing runs do not force token IDs or emit logits.",
  "kernel": "Decode only. Single query row, 32 query heads / 8 KV heads, width 64. 4096 physical KV rows, 32 splits. BF16 K/V expanded to float, FP32 simdgroup matrix multiply and partial softmax followed by the ordinary split reduction. Other shapes follow the regular dispatch.",
